    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2667" root="بصق" body-key="b">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَصَقَ</span></b> , (Lth, JK, S, K,) [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَصُقَ</span></b> ,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَصْقٌ</span>,
(S,) <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَزَقَ</span> (Lth, S, * K) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَسَقَ</span> (JK) [<i>He spat</i>]:
it is the most chaste of these three verbs. (TA in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بسق</span>.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَصَقَ فِى وَجْهِهِ</span> [lit. <i>He spat in his face,</i>]
means (assumed tropical:)  <i>he held him in contempt,</i> or <i>despised him.</i>
(TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>He milked</i> a ewe <i>when she was with
young.</i> (K.)

